      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "For the functions $g(x)$ and $u(x),$ you're given the following data:\n\n$$\ng(-2)=-6,\\,{g}^{′}(-2)=3,\\,u(-2)=4,\\,{u}^{′}(-2)=-8\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2g(x)+u(x))$ at $x=-2.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2g(x)+u(x))=2{g}^{′}(x)+{u}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-2$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2g(x)+u(x))|}_{x=-2} & =2{g}^{′}(-2)+{u}^{′}(-2) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3+(-8) \\\\  & =6-8 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
